# M5 walkthrough: schedules, approvals and the attention inbox.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the JetBrains HTTP client.
# Prerequisite: a department with a lead (see m2-org.http) and a default model (m1-providers.http).

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:4111
@token = paste-your-admin-token-here
@departmentId = paste-a-department-id
@scheduleId = paste-a-schedule-id
@attentionId = paste-an-attention-item-id-url-encoded

### Every weekday at 9:00 (your timezone from settings, unless you set one)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/schedules
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "departmentId": "{{departmentId}}",
  "title": "Morning digest",
  "brief": "Summarize what changed in AI agent frameworks since yesterday.",
  "cron": "0 9 * * 1-5"
}

### Or ask the chief: it sets up the schedule for the right department
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/agents/chief/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "Every Monday at 8:30, have research summarize the week's AI news." }],
  "memory": { "thread": "chief:main", "resource": "owner" }
}

### All schedules, with their department and next run
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/schedules
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Run one now: the task goes to the department's lead
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/schedules/{{scheduleId}}/run
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Its tasks
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks?scheduleId={{scheduleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Pause it (resume with "active"; cron and timezone can change too)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/schedules/{{scheduleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "paused" }

### Delete it (its past tasks stay)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/schedules/{{scheduleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Gate a tool: the agent pauses before each call until you approve it
### (grant tools in an agent definition, see m2-org.http)
# "tools": [{ "key": "web_search", "requireApproval": true }]

### What needs you: approvals, questions, stopped tasks, results to review, setup problems
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/attention
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Approve a call (ids contain colons: URL-encode them). Retrying with the same key is safe.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/attention/{{attentionId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: approve-1

### Or decline it: the agent is told why and carries on without it
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/attention/{{attentionId}}/decline
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: decline-1

{ "reason": "Not during the release freeze" }
